// Local development workspace for the Go SDK modules under go/.
//
// Every module in this list builds against the copy in this checkout, not the
// version its go.mod requires. That is what lets the published go.mod files
// require real versions (github.com/langwatch/scenario/go vX.Y.Z) and carry no
// replace directives: cmd/go ignores replace directives in dependencies, so a
// consumer of a submodule would otherwise resolve a version that does not exist.
//
// The replace block is pinned to the version the go.mod files require. cmd/go
// still reads the go.mod of each required version while building the module
// graph, even for a workspace module, so without it a version that is not
// tagged yet (every release pull request, and the first release) cannot be
// resolved. release-please bumps those lines together with the go.mod files
// (x-release-please-version), so they always name the version being released.
//
// The go line must stay at or above the highest go line in the modules below
// (voice/tunnel/ngrok needs 1.25.7). `make go-work-check` fails when a go.mod
// under go/ is missing from the use list. Set GOWORK=off to build a module the
// way a consumer does. See RELEASE_PLEASE.md.
go 1.25.7

use (
	.
	./examples
	./live
	./providers/anthropic
	./providers/bedrock
	./providers/gemini
	./providers/openai
	./voice
	./voice/examples
	./voice/tunnel/ngrok
)

replace (
	github.com/langwatch/scenario/go v0.1.0 => ./ // x-release-please-version
	github.com/langwatch/scenario/go/providers/openai v0.1.0 => ./providers/openai // x-release-please-version
	github.com/langwatch/scenario/go/voice v0.1.0 => ./voice // x-release-please-version
)
